IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc-interpretation.l4 -- sections 1, 2.2, 2.3, 3 and 3.01 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Split from ccc-definitions.l4 (which holds section 2 and section 2.1) for two reasons: size, and kind. These provisions are not
-- definitions: section 2.2 gives individuals a power and bars others from it, section 2.3 gives the Attorney General of Canada a power,
-- section 3 is a rule of reading, and section 3.01 extends a phrase in listed provisions. Imports the core only.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads is explained at the head of ccc-definitions.l4: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words);
-- NOTHING (not covered). A failed "if" or "where" in a provision gives JUST FALSE within that provision (a marginal reading for a lawyer:
-- NOTES.md); a limit on the purposes or provisions a grant covers, with no "only", gives NOTHING outside it.

§ `Section 1 -- Short title`

-- 1 This Act may be cited as the Criminal Code. Machinery (the Act's own short title): no rule; carried as a quotation.
-- src:11 | 1 This Act may be cited as the Criminal Code.
@ref s 1 (src:11)
`s 1 the short title` MEANS "Criminal Code"

§ `Section 2.2 -- Acting on victim’s behalf`

-- 2.2 (1) For the purposes of sections 606, 672.5, 715.37, 722, 737.1 and 745.63, any of the following individuals may act on the victim’s behalf if the victim is dead or incapable of acting on their own behalf:
-- (a) the victim’s spouse (or, if dead, their spouse at the time of death); (b) the common-law partner (likewise); (c) a relative or dependant; (d) one with custody or responsible for the care or support of the victim; (e) the same for a dependant of the victim.
-- src:229 | 2.2 (1) For the purposes of sections 606, 672.5, 715.37, 722, 737.1 and 745.63, any of the following individuals may act on the victim’s behalf if the victim is dead or incapable of acting on their own behalf:
-- src:230 | (a) the victim’s spouse, or if the victim is dead, their spouse at the time of death;
-- src:231 | (b) the victim’s common-law partner, or if the victim is dead, their common-law partner at the time of death;
-- src:232 | (c) a relative or dependant of the victim;
-- src:233 | (d) an individual who has in law or fact custody, or is responsible for the care or support, of the victim; and
-- src:234 | (e) an individual who has in law or fact custody, or is responsible for the care or support, of a dependant of the victim.
@ref s 2.2(1) (src:229-234)
DECLARE `s 2.2(1) the individual's relation to the victim` IS ONE OF
    `the victim’s spouse, or if the victim is dead, their spouse at the time of death`   -- (a)
    `the victim’s common-law partner, or if the victim is dead, their common-law partner at the time of death`   -- (b)
    `a relative or dependant of the victim`   -- (c)
    `an individual who has in law or fact custody, or is responsible for the care or support, of the victim`   -- (d)
    `an individual who has in law or fact custody, or is responsible for the care or support, of a dependant of the victim`   -- (e)
    `an individual with none of those relations to the victim`

@ref s 2.2(1) (src:229-234)
GIVEN relation IS A `s 2.2(1) the individual's relation to the victim`
      `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the individual would act` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the victim is dead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim is incapable of acting on their own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2.2(1) the individual may act on the victim’s behalf` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the purpose is one of sections 606, 672.5, 715.37, 722, 737.1 and 745.63` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of sections 606, 672.5, 715.37, 722, 737.1 and 745.63"
        IF NOT (`the victim is dead` OR `the victim is incapable of acting on their own behalf`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the victim is dead or incapable of acting on their own behalf"
        IF relation EQUALS `an individual with none of those relations to the victim` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any of the following individuals may act" lists the individuals who may and does not close the list
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the purpose is one of sections 606, 672.5, 715.37, 722, 737.1 and 745.63` MEANS
                `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the individual would act`'s `section` EQUALS 606
            OR  `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the individual would act`'s `section` EQUALS 672.5
            OR  `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the individual would act`'s `section` EQUALS 715.37
            OR  `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the individual would act`'s `section` EQUALS 722
            OR  `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the individual would act`'s `section` EQUALS 737.1
            OR  `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the individual would act`'s `section` EQUALS 745.63

-- (2) An individual is not entitled to act on a victim’s behalf if the individual is an accused in relation to the offence or alleged offence that resulted in the victim suffering harm or loss
-- or is an individual who is found guilty of that offence or who is found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial in respect of that offence.
-- The answer is "the individual is barred" (JUST TRUE) or, where none of the three facts holds, JUST FALSE (a failed "if": a marginal reading, NOTES.md).
-- src:236 | (2) An individual is not entitled to act on a victim’s behalf if the individual is an accused in relation to the offence or alleged offence that resulted in the victim suffering harm or loss or is an individual who is found guilty of that offence or who is found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial in respect of that offence.
@ref s 2.2(2) (src:236)
GIVEN `the individual is an accused in relation to the offence or alleged offence that resulted in the victim suffering harm or loss` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is found guilty of that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial in respect of that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2.2(2) the individual is not entitled to act on the victim’s behalf` MEANS
    IF     `the individual is an accused in relation to the offence or alleged offence that resulted in the victim suffering harm or loss`
        OR `the individual is found guilty of that offence`
        OR `the individual is found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial in respect of that offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the individual is an accused in relation to the offence or alleged offence that resulted in the victim suffering harm or loss" (none of the three conditions holds: a failed "if")

-- Sections 2.2(1) and 2.2(2) together: the individual may act unless subsection (2) bars them. A composition of the two functions above; it restates neither.
@ref s 2.2(2), composed with s 2.2(1) (src:236)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2.2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 2.2(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF (`the answer of s 2.2(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual is not entitled to act on a victim’s behalf if the individual is an accused in relation to the offence"
    ELSE `the answer of s 2.2(1)`   -- the grant: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE or NOTHING as subsection (1) answers

§ `Section 2.3 -- Concurrent jurisdiction`

-- 2.3 (1) The proceedings for the purposes of paragraph (a) of the definition Attorney General in section 2 are (a) to (f). The list is introduced by "are" and not closed by "only": read as closed, a marginal reading (NOTES.md).
-- src:238 | 2.3 (1) The proceedings for the purposes of paragraph (a) of the definition Attorney General in section 2 are
-- src:239 | (a) proceedings in relation to an offence under subsection 7(2.01), (2.3), (2.31), (2.35) or (2.36) or section 57, 58, 83.12, 103, 104, 121.1, 380, 382, 382.1, 391, 400, 424.1, 431.1, 467.11 or 467.111 or in relation to any terrorism offence;
-- src:240 | (b) proceedings in relation to an offence against a member of United Nations personnel or associated personnel under section 235, 236, 266 to 269, 269.1, 271 to 273, 279 or 279.1;
-- src:241 | (c) proceedings in relation to an offence referred to in subsection 7(3.71) or in relation to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1) if the act or omission constituting the offence was committed outside Canada and is deemed under any of subsections 7(2), (2.1) to (2.21), (3), (3.1), (3.72) and (3.73) to have been committed in Canada;
-- src:242 | (d) proceedings in relation to an offence if the act or omission constituting the offence is a terrorist activity referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1) and was committed outside Canada and is deemed by virtue of subsection 7(3.74) or (3.75) to have been committed in Canada;
-- src:243 | (e) a proceeding in relation to an offence under section 811 that arises out of a breach of a recognizance made under section 810.01 or 810.011, if he or she has given consent to the information referred to in those sections; and
-- src:244 | (f) proceedings under section 83.13, 83.14, 83.222, 83.223 or 83.3.
@ref s 2.3(1) (src:238-244)
DECLARE `s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings` HAS
    `the offence charged`   IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN   -- (a): "or in relation to any terrorism offence"
    `the offence is against a member of United Nations personnel or associated personnel`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `the offence is referred to in subsection 7(3.71)`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `the offence is referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1), the act or omission was committed outside Canada and is deemed under any of subsections 7(2), (2.1) to (2.21), (3), (3.1), (3.72) and (3.73) to have been committed in Canada`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `the act or omission is a terrorist activity referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1), was committed outside Canada and is deemed by subsection 7(3.74) or (3.75) to have been committed in Canada`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
    `the proceeding is in relation to an offence under section 811 that arises out of a breach of a recognizance made under section 810.01 or 810.011, and the Attorney General of Canada has given consent to the information referred to in those sections`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
    `the section the proceedings are under`   IS A `Provision of the Code`   -- (f): proceedings under a section, not an offence

@ref s 2.3(1) (src:238-244)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 2.3(1) facts of the proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)` MEANS
    IF (`limb (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `limb (b)` OR `limb (c)` OR `limb (d)` OR `limb (e)` OR `limb (f)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`limb (a)` EQUALS NOTHING)
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a terrorism offence is for s 2 "terrorism offence" and is not determined
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The proceedings for the purposes of paragraph (a) of the definition Attorney General in section 2 are" (none of (a) to (f) holds)
    WHERE
        `the offence section` MEANS facts's `the offence charged`'s `section`
        `the offence subsection` MEANS facts's `the offence charged`'s `subsection`
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            IF    (`the offence section` EQUALS 7 AND (`the offence subsection` EQUALS "(2.01)" OR `the offence subsection` EQUALS "(2.3)" OR `the offence subsection` EQUALS "(2.31)" OR `the offence subsection` EQUALS "(2.35)" OR `the offence subsection` EQUALS "(2.36)"))
               OR `the offence section` EQUALS 57 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 58 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 83.12 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 103 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 104
               OR `the offence section` EQUALS 121.1 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 380 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 382 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 382.1 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 391
               OR `the offence section` EQUALS 400 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 424.1 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 431.1 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 467.11 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 467.111
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE facts's `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
        `limb (b)` MEANS
                facts's `the offence is against a member of United Nations personnel or associated personnel`
            AND (   `the offence section` EQUALS 235 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 236
                 OR (`the offence section` AT LEAST 266 AND `the offence section` AT MOST 269)
                 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 269.1
                 OR (`the offence section` AT LEAST 271 AND `the offence section` AT MOST 273)
                 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 279 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 279.1)
        `limb (c)` MEANS facts's `the offence is referred to in subsection 7(3.71)` OR facts's `the offence is referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1), the act or omission was committed outside Canada and is deemed under any of subsections 7(2), (2.1) to (2.21), (3), (3.1), (3.72) and (3.73) to have been committed in Canada`
        `limb (d)` MEANS facts's `the act or omission is a terrorist activity referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1), was committed outside Canada and is deemed by subsection 7(3.74) or (3.75) to have been committed in Canada`
        `limb (e)` MEANS facts's `the proceeding is in relation to an offence under section 811 that arises out of a breach of a recognizance made under section 810.01 or 810.011, and the Attorney General of Canada has given consent to the information referred to in those sections`
        `the proceedings section` MEANS facts's `the section the proceedings are under`'s `section`
        `limb (f)` MEANS
            `the proceedings section` EQUALS 83.13 OR `the proceedings section` EQUALS 83.14 OR `the proceedings section` EQUALS 83.222 OR `the proceedings section` EQUALS 83.223 OR `the proceedings section` EQUALS 83.3

-- (2) For greater certainty, the Attorney General of Canada or his or her lawful deputy may, in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (1) or an offence under any Act of Parliament -- other than this Act or the Canada Elections Act -- or any regulation
-- made under such an Act, exercise all the powers and perform all the duties and functions assigned to the Attorney General by or under this Act, and those powers include the power to commence and to conduct (a) to (f).
-- src:246 | (2) For greater certainty, the Attorney General of Canada or his or her lawful deputy may, in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (1) or an offence under any Act of Parliament — other than this Act or the Canada Elections Act — or any regulation made under such an Act, exercise all the powers and perform all the duties and functions assigned to the Attorney General by or under this Act, and those powers include the power to commence and to conduct
-- src:247 | (a) a proceeding for conspiring or attempting to commit such an offence or for being an accessory after the fact or counselling a person to be a party to such an offence;
-- src:248 | (b) a proceeding in relation to a criminal organization offence that arises out of conduct that relates, in whole or in part, to any offence for which he or she has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding;
-- src:249 | (c) a proceeding in relation to an offence referred to in section 354, 355.2, 355.4 or 462.31 that arises out of conduct that relates, in whole or in part, to any offence for which he or she has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding or out of any act or omission that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted such an offence;
-- src:250 | (d) a proceeding for the breach of any court order made in the course of a proceeding commenced or conducted by him or her;
-- src:251 | (e) a proceeding for the failure to comply with any condition associated with the release of a person by a peace officer or other competent authority — including a condition to appear at a specified time and place — in relation to any offence for which he or she has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding; and
-- src:252 | (f) any ancillary proceedings in relation to any offence for which he or she has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding.
@ref s 2.3(2) (src:246-252)
DECLARE `s 2.3(2) the kind of proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `a proceeding for conspiring or attempting to commit such an offence or for being an accessory after the fact or counselling a person to be a party to such an offence`   -- (a)
    `a proceeding in relation to a criminal organization offence that arises out of conduct that relates, in whole or in part, to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding`   -- (b)
    `a proceeding in relation to an offence referred to in section 354, 355.2, 355.4 or 462.31 that arises out of conduct that relates, in whole or in part, to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding or out of any act or omission that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted such an offence`   -- (c)
    `a proceeding for the breach of any court order made in the course of a proceeding commenced or conducted by the Attorney General of Canada`   -- (d)
    `a proceeding for the failure to comply with any condition associated with the release of a person by a peace officer or other competent authority, including a condition to appear at a specified time and place, in relation to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding`   -- (e)
    `any ancillary proceedings in relation to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding`   -- (f)
    `a proceeding of another kind`

@ref s 2.3(2) (src:246)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2.3(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or the Canada Elections Act, or a regulation made under such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2.3(2) the Attorney General of Canada may exercise the powers and perform the duties and functions of the Attorney General` MEANS
    IF (`the answer of s 2.3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the offence is under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or the Canada Elections Act, or a regulation made under such an Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (1) or an offence under any Act of Parliament"

@ref s 2.3(2) (src:246-252)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2.3(2) the kind of proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2.3(2) those powers include the power to commence and to conduct the proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a proceeding for conspiring or attempting to commit such an offence or for being an accessory after the fact or counselling a person to be a party to such an offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a proceeding in relation to a criminal organization offence that arises out of conduct that relates, in whole or in part, to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a proceeding in relation to an offence referred to in section 354, 355.2, 355.4 or 462.31 that arises out of conduct that relates, in whole or in part, to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding or out of any act or omission that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted such an offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a proceeding for the breach of any court order made in the course of a proceeding commenced or conducted by the Attorney General of Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a proceeding for the failure to comply with any condition associated with the release of a person by a peace officer or other competent authority, including a condition to appear at a specified time and place, in relation to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any ancillary proceedings in relation to any offence for which the Attorney General of Canada has the power to commence and to conduct a proceeding` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a proceeding of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "those powers include"

-- (3) For greater certainty, in respect of an offence under the Canada Elections Act, the Director of Public Prosecutions, subject to the Director of Public Prosecutions Act, exercises the powers and performs the duties and functions of the Attorney General of Canada referred to in subsection (2).
-- "Subject to the Director of Public Prosecutions Act" points outside the sources and is not encoded.
-- src:254 | (3) For greater certainty, in respect of an offence under the Canada Elections Act, the Director of Public Prosecutions, subject to the Director of Public Prosecutions Act, exercises the powers and performs the duties and functions of the Attorney General of Canada referred to in subsection (2).
@ref s 2.3(3) (src:254)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence under the Canada Elections Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2.3(3) the Director of Public Prosecutions exercises the powers and performs the duties and functions of the Attorney General of Canada` MEANS
    IF `the offence is an offence under the Canada Elections Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an offence under the Canada Elections Act"

§ `Section 3 -- Descriptive cross-references`

-- 3 Where, in any provision of this Act, a reference to another provision of this Act or a provision of any other Act is followed by words in parenthesis that are or purport to be descriptive of the subject-matter of the provision referred to,
-- the words in parenthesis form no part of the provision in which they occur but shall be deemed to have been inserted for convenience of reference only.
-- A rule of reading over a small typed representation of a reference. "Where" failing gives JUST FALSE within this section (the periods and "where" ruling of 2026-11-05).
-- src:256 | 3 Where, in any provision of this Act, a reference to another provision of this Act or a provision of any other Act is followed by words in parenthesis that are or purport to be descriptive of the subject-matter of the provision referred to, the words in parenthesis form no part of the provision in which they occur but shall be deemed to have been inserted for convenience of reference only.
@ref s 3 (src:256)
DECLARE `s 3 reference` HAS
    `it is in a provision of this Act`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a reference to another provision of this Act or to a provision of any other Act`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is followed by words in parenthesis`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the words are or purport to be descriptive of the subject-matter of the provision referred to`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 3 (src:256)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 3 reference`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 the words in parenthesis form no part of the provision and are deemed inserted for convenience of reference only` MEANS
    IF     reference's `it is in a provision of this Act`
       AND reference's `it is a reference to another provision of this Act or to a provision of any other Act`
       AND reference's `it is followed by words in parenthesis`
       AND reference's `the words are or purport to be descriptive of the subject-matter of the provision referred to`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in any provision of this Act, a reference to another provision of this Act or a provision of any other Act is followed by words in parenthesis that are or purport to be descriptive of the subject-matter of the provision referred to" (a failed "where")

§ `Section 3.01 -- Violence in commission of offence, including against intimate partner`

-- 3.01 (2) Subsection (1) applies with respect to (a) subsection 109(1); (b) subsections 110(1) and (2.1); (b.1) subsection 263.1(1); (c) subsections 515(3), (4.1), (4.3) and (6); (d) subsection 718.3(8); (e) section 726.21; and (f) subsection 810.03(4).
-- The list names provisions and does not say "only": a provision outside it is NOT COVERED (the scope-limit ruling of 2026-11-05, (c)).
-- src:264 | (2) Subsection (1) applies with respect to
-- src:265 | (a) subsection 109(1);
-- src:266 | (b) subsections 110(1) and (2.1);
-- src:267 | (b.1) subsection 263.1(1);
-- src:268 | (c) subsections 515(3), (4.1), (4.3) and (6);
-- src:269 | (d) subsection 718.3(8);
-- src:270 | (e) section 726.21; and
-- src:271 | (f) subsection 810.03(4).
@ref s 3.01(2) (src:264-271)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3.01(2) subsection (1) applies with respect to the provision` MEANS
    IF     (provision's `section` EQUALS 109 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
        OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 110 AND (provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(2.1)"))
        OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 263.1 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
        OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 515 AND (provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(3)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(4.1)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(4.3)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(6)"))
        OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 718.3 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(8)")
        OR provision's `section` EQUALS 726.21
        OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 810.03 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(4)")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) applies with respect to" the listed provisions

-- 3.01 (1) In a provision listed in subsection (2), a reference to an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons includes a reference to any of the following offences:
-- (a) an offence that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose; (b) an offence under section 264 (criminal harassment); (c) an offence under section 279.01 (trafficking in persons); (d) an offence under section 279.011 (trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years).
-- src:258 | 3.01 (1) In a provision listed in subsection (2), a reference to an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons includes a reference to any of the following offences:
-- src:259 | (a) an offence that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose;
-- src:260 | (b) an offence under section 264 (criminal harassment);
-- src:261 | (c) an offence under section 279.01 (trafficking in persons);
-- src:262 | (d) an offence under section 279.011 (trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years).
@ref s 3.01(1) (src:258-262)
DECLARE `s 3.01(1) the offence` IS ONE OF
    `an offence that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose`   -- (a)
    `an offence under section 264 (criminal harassment)`   -- (b)
    `an offence under section 279.01 (trafficking in persons)`   -- (c)
    `an offence under section 279.011 (trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years)`   -- (d)
    `an offence that is none of those`

@ref s 3.01(1) (src:258-262)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 3.01(1) the offence`
      `the answer of s 3.01(2) for the provision being applied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the answer of s 3.01(2) for the provision being applied` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a provision listed in subsection (2)"
    ELSE CONSIDER offence
         WHEN `an offence that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an offence under section 264 (criminal harassment)` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an offence under section 279.01 (trafficking in persons)` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an offence under section 279.011 (trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years)` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an offence that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to any of the following offences"
